<title>RUSSIA: Russia's vodka tsar dies of liver disease.</title>
<headline>Russia's vodka tsar dies of liver disease.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of Moscow's Kristall vodka factory, one of the main producers of Russia's national drink, died on Monday of cirrhosis of the liver, a source at the plant told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Vladimir Yamnikov had run the drinks combine since Soviet days, producing famous brands including Stolichnaya vodka.</p>
<p>At 56, he was two years short of the Russian man's average life expectancy -- a term considerably shorter than the European norm due, at least in part, to an average male consumption of about a quarter litre (half pint) of vodka a day.</p>
</text>
